  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Which of the following statements are correct ?</p><p>(A) Both <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>LiCl</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>MgCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> are soluble in ethanol.</p><p>(B) The oxides <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Li</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>MgO</mi></math> combine with excess of oxygen to give superoxide.</p><p>(C) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>LiF</mi></math> is less soluble in water than other alkali metal fluorides.</p><p>(D)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Li</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> is more soluble in water than other alkali metal oxides.</p><p>Choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below</p>"
  },
