  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>(A) Both <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>LiCl</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>MgCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> have covalent character so soluble in ethanol.</p><p>(C) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>LiF</mi></math> have low solubility due to high lattice&nbsp;energy.</p><p>So these two statements are correct. And other two statements are wrong.&nbsp;</p><p>Since,</p><p>(B) Li and Mg do not form superoxide</p><p>(D) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Li</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>&nbsp;is least soluble in water than other alkali metal oxides&nbsp;</p>"
